+# AthenIQ Plus — products, setup and submission
+
+The app is free. **AthenIQ Plus** is an auto-renewable subscription that adds
+the tools a phone can offer a student: the whole library offline, an AI study
+coach, and study analytics. Nothing already in the free tier is taken away.
+
+| | Free | Plus |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Browse the catalog | yes | yes |
+| Enroll in a free course and read every lesson | yes | yes |
+| Progress and certificates | yes | yes |
+| Courses kept offline | 1 | unlimited |
+| AI study coach | — | yes |
+| Study analytics (pace, remaining work, weak modules) | — | yes |
+| Registrar queue priority for certificate requests | — | yes |
+
+## Products
+
+Create these in App Store Connect and Google Play Console, then point a
+RevenueCat project at both stores.
+
+| Product id | Type | Duration | Price (USD) |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `institute.atheniq.plus.monthly` | auto-renewable | 1 month | 9.99 |
+| `institute.atheniq.plus.yearly` | auto-renewable | 1 year | 79.99 |
+
+Both belong to one subscription group, `AthenIQ Plus`, so a learner can move
+between them without being subscribed twice. The yearly product is 33% cheaper
+than twelve months — say so in the App Store "promotional text", not as a fake
+discount.
+
+The Android products use the same ids and the same base prices; Play converts
+to local currency.
+
+### Trial
+
+If an introductory offer is wanted, configure **7 days free on the yearly
+product only** in App Store Connect and Play Console. Do not hard-code a trial
+in the app: the store reports eligibility, and RevenueCat carries it.
+
+## RevenueCat
+
+1. Create a project, add the iOS app (`institute.atheniq.app`) and the Android
+   app (`institute.atheniq.app`).
+2. Add the two products, then an entitlement named **`plus`** attached to both.
+3. Add one offering, `default`, with a `$rc_monthly` and `$rc_annual` package
+   mapped to the products above. The paywall reads `offerings.current`.
+4. Copy the **public** SDK keys into the mobile build environment:
+   - `EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_IOS_KEY`
+   - `EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_ANDROID_KEY`
+5. Create a **secret** API key (V1, read access is enough) and a webhook:
+   - Console: `REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY`, `REVENUECAT_ENTITLEMENT_ID=plus`
+   - Webhook URL: `https://registrar.atheniq.institute/api/internal/revenuecat/webhook`
+   - Webhook authorization header: `Bearer <REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN>`, and the
+     same value in the console environment.
+   - Send all events; the handler treats renewals, expirations, cancellations,
+     pauses and refunds explicitly.
+
+The console never trusts the phone. `POST /api/mobile/v1/premium/sync` asks
+RevenueCat for the learner's entitlements using the secret key; only an
+entitlement named `plus` becomes a membership row. Without
+`REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY` the route answers `503 storeConfigured:false` and
+grants nothing.
+
+## App configuration
+
+`app.json` carries version `1.1.0` / iOS build `2` / Android `versionCode 2`.
+`eas.json` has development, preview and production profiles plus a submit block
+for App Store and Play.
+
+```bash
+npx eas-cli build --platform ios --profile production
+npx eas-cli build --platform android --profile production
+npx eas-cli submit --platform ios --profile production
+npx eas-cli submit --platform android --profile production
+```
+
+RevenueCat and StoreKit/Play Billing are native modules: Expo Go cannot take a
+payment. Use a development build (`--profile development`) to test sandbox
+purchases, restore, renewal, cancellation and refund before submitting.
+
+## App Review notes
+
+Paste into "Notes for Review":
+
+> AthenIQ Plus is an auto-renewable subscription sold in the app: monthly
+> (institute.atheniq.plus.monthly) and yearly (institute.atheniq.plus.yearly).
+> The app is fully usable for free; Plus adds offline downloads beyond one
+> course, an AI study coach and study analytics. Sign in with the sandbox
+> learner account in the review notes; the paywall is on Account → Upgrade to
+> AthenIQ Plus. Restore Purchases is on the same screen. Terms:
+> https://atheniq.institute/terms · Privacy: https://atheniq.institute/privacy
+
+Apple requires the paywall to show the subscription title, length and price,
+that payment is charged to the Apple account, that it renews unless cancelled
+24 hours before the end, and links to Terms (EULA) and Privacy. The screen has
+all four.
+
+## Submission checklist
+
+- [ ] Both products created and "Ready to Submit" with localised display names
+- [ ] Subscription group and both products attached to entitlement `plus`
+- [ ] Offering `default` has monthly and yearly packages
+- [ ] `EXPO_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_*` keys in the production build env
+- [ ] Console has `REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY` and `REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN`
+- [ ] Webhook reachable and returning 200 for a test event
+- [ ] Sandbox purchase, restore, renewal, cancellation, refund all observed
+- [ ] Free tier still reads every lesson of an enrolled free course
+- [ ] Screenshots include the paywall and the plan row in Account
+- [ ] Privacy nutrition label: purchases (not linked to tracking), identifiers
+- [ ] App Review notes pasted; demo learner account credentials supplied
